For Claude (and all AI sessions): Read this file first before making any changes. It is the single source of truth for this project.1. Project SummaryAniList Metro is a single-file (index.html) Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS web application that provides a Windows Phone 7 / Zune HD / Windows 8–style interface for the AniList anime/manga tracking platform. It is AMOLED-optimized, strictly Metro-designed, and authentication-aware.Main file: /Users/BrijeshKrishnan/BRIJESH KRISHNAN/projectgobrr/index.htmlStack: Vanilla HTML5 + CSS3 + ES6+ JavaScript — no build tools, no Node, no frameworkAPI: AniList GraphQL v2 — https://graphql.anilist.coExternal CDN: FontAwesome 6.4.0 (Icons)Reference Framework: Metro UI CSS v4 (Translating its DOM structures and CSS paradigms into our Vanilla stack).Sounds: xbox360 metro soundeffects/ directory (.wav files via Web Audio API)2. The Prime Directive — Metro UI v4 Design BibleYou are an expert Frontend Engineer specializing in the Metro design language heavily influenced by Metro UI CSS v4. You MUST strictly follow these rules in every edit.2.1 Core Geometry & Philosophyborder-radius: 0 !important — zero rounded corners, everywhere, always.box-shadow: none !important — zero shadows, ever. (Exception: deep layering in modals can use a very harsh, unblurred 10px solid black/dark overlay, but no CSS drop-shadows).Content over Chrome: Typography and spacing do the heavy lifting. Borders are almost non-existent.Flawless responsiveness: Grid systems must be rigidly mathematically aligned.2.2 Complete Metro v4 Color PaletteThe app utilizes pure black for AMOLED, but components map to the expanded Metro v4 color system.CSS/* Base Backgrounds */
